{
  "$comment": [
    "The payload file list, machine-readable. This is the single store of WHICH",
    "upstream files the normal workflow may install into a target repo; payload-manifest.md beside it",
    "holds the reasoning and the exclusions \u2014 everything a flat",
    "list cannot carry. Adding a payload file means adding it here once: the",
    "installing agent reads this, and so does scripts/check-payload-links.mjs.",
    "",
    "Categories group the payload. Every install starts from an empty folder and",
    "takes every category: 'core', 'ui', 'pack', and 'scaffold'.",
    "",
    "Paths use the logical .claude/ form. A target stores them in a real .agents/",
    "folder with .claude and .codex links to it, so .claude/hooks.json is also",
    "the .codex/hooks.json that Codex reads.",
    "",
    "skillDirs are directory names under .claude/skills/, copied whole (references/",
    "and scripts/ included). dirs are copied whole from the repo root. Anything in",
    "'exclude' is removed after its directory is walked."
  ],
